<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Calvi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1794">1794</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of Calvi was fought from June to August 1794, when British forces and Corsican allies besieged the French garrison of Calvi in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corsica">Corsica</a>. Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> commanded naval guns ashore and lost the sight of his right eye from flying debris. The French surrender completed the expulsion of French forces from the island and secured the Anglo-Corsican Kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-calvi.jpg" alt="Siege of Calvi" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bowyer, Robert, Worthington, William Henry &amp; Bromley, William, 1808 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nelson_at_Calvi_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
